<SiteLayout title="Editorial Policy: Sources, Corrections and Updates" description="How 8PayCommission sources facts, labels projections, reviews pages and handles corrections. Read this before relying on a calculator or estimate." slug="editorial-policy" h1="Editorial Policy" lead="How we source facts, label projections and fix mistakes." faq={faq} toc={toc} related={related} pageType="info" breadcrumbLabel="Editorial Policy">

<h2 id="sources">Sources we use</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Primary:</strong> Gazette notifications, Cabinet decisions, PIB releases, Finance Ministry and DoPT office memorandums, replies in Parliament, and 8cpc.gov.in.</li>
<li><strong>Secondary:</strong> Established news organisations, used to confirm dates and figures when a primary source is not public.</li>
<li><strong>Not used:</strong> Unsourced social media posts, forwarded messages and anonymous claims.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="labels">Facts, scenarios and projections</h2>
<p>Every page separates confirmed facts from assumptions. Figures such as 1.92, 2.28 or 2.86 for the fitment factor are labelled scenarios. Calculators state their assumptions beside the result.</p>
<h2 id="updates">Updates</h2>
<p>Pages carry a last-updated date. We review key pages when a new order or Cabinet decision is announced, and at least every quarter.</p>
<h2 id="corrections">Corrections</h2>
<p>If you find an error, email <a href="mailto:dailylifetech.official@gmail.com">dailylifetech.official@gmail.com</a> with the page address and a source. We correct confirmed errors promptly and note material changes on the page.</p>
<h2 id="advice">Not professional advice</h2>
<p>Our content is general information. It is not financial, legal or tax advice. Follow your department orders for decisions about your pay and benefits.</p>

</SiteLayout>
